      "writtenOn": "2022-07-05T06:47:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Target to have a backtrace in bootloader for debugging as watchdog reset, like\n\nBacktrace Core 0\nPC: do_irq_disabled_deadloop+0x28 [debug_reboot] \u003cFFFFFFC009CFB2D8\u003e\nLR: do_irq_disabled_deadloop+0x28 [debug_reboot] \u003cFFFFFFC009CFB2D8\u003e\n\n[\u003cFFFFFFC009CFB2D8\u003e] do_irq_disabled_deadloop+0x28 [debug_reboot]\n[\u003cFFFFFFC01023592C\u003e] multi_cpu_stop+0x11c\n[\u003cFFFFFFC010236224\u003e] cpu_stopper_thread+0xf8\n[\u003cFFFFFFC010165234\u003e] smpboot_thread_fn+0x2b4\n[\u003cFFFFFFC01015C4E0\u003e] kthread+0x158\n[\u003cFFFFFFC010015118\u003e] ret_from_fork+0x10\n\nIf we want to achieve this, for embeded module kallsym.cwe need to know module\nkallsym for embedded modules\nmodule kallsyms for loaded modules\n \nCurrent rom, module kallsyms parser in bootloader is not workable(UNKNOWN+0x0) like b/237554648 because both module list_find and kallsyms_lookup_name are no longer supported.\nex.\n  Backtrace Core 0\n  PC: UNKNOWN+0x0 \u003cFFFFFFC00964E25C\u003e\n  LR: UNKNOWN+0x0 \u003cFFFFFFC00964E25C\u003e\n\n  [\u003cFFFFFFC00964E25C\u003e] UNKNOWN+0x0\n  [\u003cFFFFFFC00964E278\u003e] UNKNOWN+0x0\n  [\u003cFFFFFFC010160BB0\u003e] multi_cpu_stop+0xf8\n  [\u003cFFFFFFC010161254\u003e] cpu_stopper_thread+0xc4\n  [\u003cFFFFFFC0100B22A0\u003e] smpboot_thread_fn+0x1fc\n  [\u003cFFFFFFC0100AC758\u003e] kthread+0x13c\n  [\u003cFFFFFFC010005DE0\u003e] ret_from_fork+0x10\n\nSo bootloader needs a module list head or latch tree root address to lookup it.\n- static LIST_HEAD(modules);\n- static struct mod_tree_root {\n\u003e---struct latch_tree_root root;\n\u003e---unsigned long addr_min;\n\u003e---unsigned long addr_max;\n} mod_tree",
      "parentUuid": "96bf890f_8af2e562",
